# Page & API auth guards

Never ship a protected route that only hides UI on the client. Direct URL entry must fail closed.

## Layers (all required for protected areas)

1. **`src/proxy.ts`** — optimistic cookie check (`getSessionCookie`). Redirect to `/login?next=…` if missing. No DB here.
2. **Server layout / page** — `requireServerUser` or `requireServerSuperAdmin` from `@/lib/server-auth` (Better Auth session + DB role). This is the real page gate.
3. **API** — same rule on every mutating/sensitive endpoint (`requireSuperAdmin`, `requireSessionUserId`, entitlement checks). UI gates never replace API gates.

## Route map

| Path | Gate |
|------|------|
| `/` | public |
| `/login` | public; server layout redirects if already signed in |
| `/account/**` | proxy + `requireServerUser` |
| `/admin/**` | proxy + `requireServerSuperAdmin` (superadmin only) |
| `/api/admin/**` | `requireSuperAdmin` |
| `/api/ai/keys/**`, `/api/me` | authenticated session |

## When adding a page

```tsx
// src/app/secret/layout.tsx
import { requireServerUser } from "@/lib/server-auth";

export default async function Layout({ children }) {
  await requireServerUser("/secret");
  return children;
}
```

Also extend `src/proxy.ts` `matcher` + `needsAuth` for that path.

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client-only; HTML/JS still loads on direct URL
useEffect(() => {
  authClient.getSession().then(/* setDenied */);
}, []);

// ✅ GOOD — server layout blocks render + redirect
await requireServerSuperAdmin("/admin");
```

- Do not rely on `AdminGate` / AuthBar visibility alone.
- Do not put DB session lookups in `proxy.ts` (keep optimistic).
- Role `admin` ≠ console access; console is `superadmin` only unless product changes both UI and `requireSuperAdmin`.
- Guest ↔ `/login` must use **hard** `<a href>` (not Next `<Link>`). Soft nav leaves the home `app.js` shell half-mounted (missing topbar/status / stale portals).
